      "version": "0.1.0",
      "description": "Before you file a patent, ship a feature, or pitch an invention, check whether it's already patented. Don't already know what to search for? The patent_scan prompt scans your own codebase and docs, surfaces the distinct technical mechanisms in it, and checks each one against prior art automatically — you don't need to already know what's patentable to find out. Patlas searches real USPTO and EPO/Espacenet patent data and grounds every AI-generated similarity claim or claim-quote in the actual retrieved text — no invented patent IDs, no fabricated quotes, no infringement/patentability verdicts. Typical calls: search_prior_art (\"has anything like this wireless-charging alignment mechanism already been patented?\"), compare_claims (\"compare my invention element-by-element against patent US1234567's claims\"), get_patent_detail (full text/claims/status for a known patent ID), landscape_summary (assignee/filing-trend/CPC-class stats for a technology area, computed deterministically, not estimated by the model).",
